### qAcademy API — example requests
### Works out of the box with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client)
### or IntelliJ IDEA's built-in HTTP Client. Run the app first: mvn spring-boot:run

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8085

### 1. Login as admin — copy the "token" from the response into @adminToken below
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### 2. Login as staff
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "staff",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### 3. Register a new account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "newuser",
  "password": "Pass1234",
  "role": "Staff"
}

### --- Paste a token from step 1 or 2 here, then the requests below will work ---
@adminToken = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### 4. List all students (open — no token needed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/student

### 5. Get a single student by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/student/1

### 6. Create a student (requires Admin or Staff token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/student
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "firstName": "Ada",
  "lastName": "Lovelace",
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "dateOfBirth": "10/12/1815"
}

### 7. List all courses (open)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/course

### 8. Create a course (requires Admin token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/course
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "name": "Introduction to Algorithms",
  "credits": 4
}

### 9. List all enrollments (open)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollment

### 10. Get all enrollments for one student
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollment/student/1

### 11. Enroll a student in a course (requires Admin or Staff token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollment
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "studentId": 1,
  "courseId": 1
}

### 12. Assign/update a grade (requires Admin or Staff token) — replace {id} with a real enrollment id
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollment/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "grade": "A"
}

### 13. Delete a student (requires Admin token) — replace {id} with a real student id
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/student/999
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
